              "<table class=\"answer-table\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:1rem 0;\"><thead><tr style=\"background:rgba(217,119,6,0.15); text-align:left;\"><th style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Analytical Feature</th><th style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Nation</th><th style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">State</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\"><strong>1. Fundamental Nature</strong></td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Psychological, cultural, and subjective community of sentiment.</td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Legal, political, and objective sovereign organization.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\"><strong>2. Requirement of Territory</strong></td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Can exist in diaspora without a fixed territory (e.g., Jewish people prior to 1948).</td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Definite, clearly demarcated geographic territory is strictly mandatory.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\"><strong>3. Sovereignty & Coercion</strong></td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Lacks coercive legal authority; relies on moral and psychological bonds.</td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Possesses absolute sovereignty and the monopoly of legitimate physical force.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\"><strong>4. Historical Origin</strong></td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Evolves organically over centuries through shared cultural memory.</td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">Can be created consciously or reconstituted overnight by treaty or constitution.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\"><strong>5. Plurality vs. Singularity</strong></td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">A single nation may be dispersed across multiple states.</td><td style=\"padding:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">A single state may be multinational (containing several nations).</td></tr></tbody></table>"
