              "The political vitality of any regime depends on how these three elements interact:<br/>• <strong>Power + Legitimacy = Authority:</strong> When power is legitimized by the moral consent of the community, it becomes authority.<br/>• <strong>Authority - Legitimacy = Coercive Tyranny:</strong> When a government loses its legitimacy (e.g., through corruption, fraud, or human rights abuses), its authority collapses. It can no longer rely on voluntary obedience and must fall back on naked police power and terror to survive.<br/>• <strong>Legitimacy without Power = Impotence:</strong> An exiled democratic leader may possess immense moral legitimacy, but without power (control over the state apparatus), they cannot enforce a single law."
